SIM-12: keep the default quality and rule steps at 1 second or more

adjustdata() sets a missing quality or rule time step to Hstep/10 with
integer division, which is 0 for a hydraulic step under 10 s. A quality
step of 0 makes nextqual() loop forever, and a rule step of 0 divides
by zero in ruletimestep(). Use at least 1 s for both defaults, and make
ruletimestep() fall back to one evaluation per time step if the rule
step is still not positive. EN_settimeparam already rejects 0 for both.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-12_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..46b832e 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -841,8 +841,9 @@ void  ruletimestep(Project *pr, long *tstep)
     tnow = time->Htime;
     tmax = tnow + *tstep;
 
-    // If no rules, then time increment equals current time step
-    if (net->Nrules == 0)
+    // If no rules (or no rule time step), then time increment
+    // equals current time step
+    if (net->Nrules == 0 || time->Rulestep <= 0)
     {
         dt = *tstep;
         dt1 = dt;
